* ASP.NET MVC is one of the ASP.NET products based on the Model-View-Controller (MVC) architectural pattern.

* Model: Represents the database table as a class.

* View: Defines the HTML structure for displaying data.

* Controller: Manages request handling and business logic.

!* Controllers must inherit from the Controller class and include public non-static functions known as actions.

* Five main CRUD actions: GetAll, GetById, Update, Delete, Add.

