* Two primary web application types: Multiple Page Applications (MPA) and Single Page Applications (SPA).

* ASP.NET Core is a cross-platform framework supporting Windows, Linux, and macOS.

* Internet Information Services (IIS) is the default web server for ASP.NET on Windows.

* Kestrel is an internal web server used in ASP.NET Core applications.

* Reverse Proxy Servers (Apache/Nginx) can be used for better performance and security.

* HTTP is the communication protocol between the client and server.

==>HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol)
    	is an application protocol for distributed, collaborative, and hypermedia information systems

* HTTP responses include a status code, message, and content type.

* Uniform Resource Identifiers (URIs) consist of URLs and URNs.

* System.Web is the base class library for traditional ASP.NET applications.

* Deployment can be done with IIS for ASP.NET MVC or using Kestrel with a reverse proxy in ASP.NET Core.

* Templates exist for creating empty projects or structured MVC projects with Controllers, Views, and Models folders.
